---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  kicker="Legal"
  path="/privacy/"
  updated={new Date('2026-09-26')}
  description={`What ${SITE.name} collects when you visit, subscribe or contact us, why, and what you can do about it.`}
>
  <h2>What do we collect?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Forms.</strong> If you subscribe to the newsletter or use the contact form, we store what you type (such as your email address and message). Forms are processed by our host, Netlify.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> If analytics is enabled we use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages and outbound links are used. It sets cookies and records information such as pages viewed, approximate location and device type. We do not use it to identify you.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising.</strong> If display ads are shown, Google AdSense and its partners may use cookies to show ads based on your visits to this and other sites. You can manage personalised advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Google Ad Settings</a> and read how Google uses data at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>. Visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland are asked for consent before personalised ads are shown.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host keeps standard access logs (IP address, browser, time) for security and reliability.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens when I click a partner link?</h2>
  <p>
    You are redirected to the vendor. The vendor or its affiliate network may set a cookie so that
    a sign-up can be credited to us. Their own privacy policy applies from that point.
  </p>

  <h2>How long is data kept, and who sees it?</h2>
  <p>
    Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Contact messages are kept as long as needed
    to reply. We do not sell personal data. Service providers (Netlify, Google, and any email tool we
    use) process data on our behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>What are my rights?</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR or California's CCPA/CPRA) you can ask
    for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to processing. Use the
    <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and we will respond within 30 days. You can also block
    cookies in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is written for business owners and is not directed at children under 16.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.</p>
</ProseLayout>
